module

public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.Presentation.GroupPresentation

/-!
# A transcribed presentation of the Suzuki sporadic group

This file carries the `Suz` row of the sporadic presentation data required by milestone S1 of
`TauCetiRoadmap/CFSGStatement/README.md`. It records the presentation `GPLTable.Suz.1` from
Rolf Lindenbergh's Group Presentations Library as a `TauCeti.GroupPresentation`, together with
the exact source, generator convention, transcription notes, expected counts, and decidable
checks on the transcription.

The presentation uses the Coxeter graph

```text
  a --5-- b --3-- c --8-- d --3-- e
  b --3-- f --4-- g --3-- b
```

where every generator is an involution and every omitted edge has label `2`. In particular, the
graph contributes seven square relations and one product-order relation for each of the twenty-one
unordered pairs of generators. The labels in the display are the source's path strings
`a5b3c8d3e,b3f4g3b`; the second string is the triangle on `b`, `f`, and `g` and is not joined to
`c`.

The source then appends the six relations

```text
a = (cd)^4,  a = (fg)^2,  (abcf)^5,  (bfg)^5,
((bcdcd)^5 e)^3,  (abcg)^5.
```

The last relation occupies the source record's `presdef[4]` field. The library initialization
includes that field when its `GPL_PCE` option is true, and version 1.0 sets this option to true by
default, so it belongs to the default full presentation transcribed here. The equality decoder in
the same source compiles `x = y` as `x⁻¹y`; that convention determines the first two extra words.

There are therefore `7 + 21 + 6 = 34` relators, and the metadata theorem checks that count. A count
does not see a relator exchanged for another of the same shape, so the compiled words are also
spelled out one signed letter at a time, and the per-relator lengths, the total length `275` and
the cyclic-reduction check are stated against that spelling rather than against the sealed record.
Both lengths are derived transcription checks: the source publishes no presentation length to
compare them with. An independent read-through of the version 1.0 `GPLTable.Suz.1` record and its
`DeCoxList`, `MakeWordList`, and `InitializeGroupPresentationGPL` decoders checked the generator
order, both Coxeter paths, all six appended relations, and the compiled signed letters below. As a
separate consistency check, GAP 4.15.1 enumerates `1782` cosets of the subgroup generated by `a`
through `f`, which the GPL record labels `G2(4)`. These checks are transcription provenance rather
than Lean theorems: no order, finiteness, simplicity, or identification result is asserted here.
The independent comparison below identifies this permutation image with the `FiniteSimpleGroups`
construction of `Suz`; it too is a review artifact rather than a theorem in this module.

## Independent source-to-compiled audit record

This audit was performed from the GPL artifact independently of the original transcription. The
retrieved version 1.0 `gpl.g` bytes have SHA-256
`8b90a7a65317a585b5b74d015083bd2fa3db8a969c117a220d00d7e8773103c8`. The source record is

```text
presdef := [ "a5b3c8d3e,b3f4g3b", ,
  "a=(cd)^4,a=(fg)^2,(abcf)^5,(bfg)^5,((bcdcd)^5e)^3", "(abcg)^5" ]
```

and the decoder comparison with `suzPresentation_relatorLetters` is:

* entries 1--7 are the squares of `a,b,c,d,e,f,g` inserted by `AddTrivialRelations`;
* entries 8--14 are `(ab)^5,(bc)^3,(cd)^8,(de)^3,(bf)^3,(fg)^4,(gb)^3`, the seven
  labeled edges of the two paths;
* entries 15--28 are the exponent-two relations on the fourteen complementary pairs
  `ac,ad,ae,af,ag,bd,be,ce,cf,cg,df,dg,ef,eg` inserted by `AddNonEdgeRelations`;
* entries 29--33 are the five comma-separated words in `presdef[3]`, with `MakeWordList`
  decoding the two equalities as `a⁻¹(cd)^4` and `a⁻¹(fg)^2`; and
* entry 34 is `(abcg)^5` from `presdef[4]`, included by
  `InitializeGroupPresentationGPL` because version 1.0 sets `GPL_PCE := true`.

Expanding these powers gives exactly the signed lists in `suzPresentation_relatorLetters`; no
source letter, pair relation, or optional relation differs from that theorem. This itemized record
is the independent source-to-Lean review artifact; the theorem remains the kernel-checked target
against which it was read.

## Independent comparison with `FiniteSimpleGroups`

The independent comparison used `finite-simple-groups-lean` at commit
`7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`. From the GPL presentation above, SymPy's
Todd--Coxeter implementation enumerated the cosets of `⟨a,b,c,d,e,f⟩`. It completed at
exactly `1782` cosets; the induced action satisfies all thirty-four source relators, and the point
stabilizer has suborbits of sizes `1`, `416`, and `1365`. Developing the `416`-point suborbit gives
a `416`-regular orbital graph on those `1782` cosets.

That graph was compared with the `1782`-vertex graph encoded by
`FiniteSimpleGroups.Sporadic.Suz.SuzMask`. A vertex-coloured canonical labelling, distinguishing
the base vertex and one neighbour, produced an isomorphism; every one of the `1782 * 416` directed
adjacencies was then checked under it. Transporting the seven GPL permutations across this
isomorphism produced seven even involutions preserving the encoded graph and still satisfying all
thirty-four relators. Finally, direct Schreier--Sims membership checks put all seven transported
permutations in the subgroup generated by `SuzPerm.suza` through `SuzPerm.suzf`, and put all six
of those generators in the subgroup generated by the transported permutations. Both generated
groups have order `448345497600`, agreeing with `FiniteSimpleGroups`' theorem `card_Suz`.

The computation used Python 3.14.6, SymPy 1.14.0, and pynauty 2.8.8.1. For a compact check on the
transport step, concatenating the seven image tables in generator order, with every image encoded
as a two-byte little-endian integer, has SHA-256
`30670ef2e7e902035636fa63568ef957a91fea59d4536f6d2c431dc9448b8cd7`; the corresponding
concatenation of the six pinned `FiniteSimpleGroups` tables has SHA-256
`75a378c50ccaad53155d65869595601436384ecd59eecc73fb02e22e59ef972b`. This is the roadmap's
independent comparison artifact; no external code or generated permutation table is imported into
Tau Ceti.

## Main definition

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation`: the GPL finite presentation of the Suzuki sporadic group.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_transcribed` and
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_relatorLetters`: the thirty-four relator expressions, and the
  signed letters they compile to.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_matchesMetadata`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_map_length_relators`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_totalLength` and
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation_relatorsCyclicallyReduced`: the decidable checks on the
  transcribed data, namely its two counts, its per-relator letter counts, their total, and cyclic
  reducedness of every compiled word.

## References

* R. Lindenbergh, *Group Presentations Library*, version 1.0, record `GPLTable.Suz.1`,
  <https://doris.tudelft.nl/~rlindenbergh/GPL/gpl.g>.
* C. E. Praeger and L. H. Soicher, *Low Rank Representations and Graphs for Sporadic Groups*,
  Cambridge University Press, 1997, Chapter 4, doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526039.005.
* KitaKen1, *FiniteSimpleGroups*, Suzuki construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.Sporadic

private abbrev a : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 0

private abbrev b : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 1

private abbrev c : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 2

private abbrev d : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 3

private abbrev e : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 4

private abbrev f : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 5

private abbrev g : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 6

@[inherit_doc Relator.mul]
local infixl:70 " ⬝ " => Relator.mul

/-- The seven involution relations and the twenty-one pair relations decoded from the two Coxeter
paths `a5b3c8d3e` and `b3f4g3b` in `GPLTable.Suz.1`.

The fourteen nonedges are written explicitly with exponent two, so this list records the complete
Coxeter matrix rather than relying on an implicit default. -/
private def suzCoxeterRelators : List (Relator (Fin 7)) :=
  [ .pow a 2,
    .pow b 2,
    .pow c 2,
    .pow d 2,
    .pow e 2,
    .pow f 2,
    .pow g 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ b) 5,
    .pow (b ⬝ c) 3,
    .pow (c ⬝ d) 8,
    .pow (d ⬝ e) 3,
    .pow (b ⬝ f) 3,
    .pow (f ⬝ g) 4,
    .pow (g ⬝ b) 3,
    .pow (a ⬝ c) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ d) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ e) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ g) 2,
    .pow (b ⬝ d) 2,
    .pow (b ⬝ e) 2,
    .pow (c ⬝ e) 2,
    .pow (c ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (c ⬝ g) 2,
    .pow (d ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (d ⬝ g) 2,
    .pow (e ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (e ⬝ g) 2 ]

/-- The six words following the Coxeter paths in `GPLTable.Suz.1`.

The source decoder represents an equality `x = y` by the relator `x⁻¹y`, explaining the leading
inverses in the first two entries. The final entry is the source's optional PCE relation, included
by the library's version 1.0 default. -/
private def suzAdditionalRelators : List (Relator (Fin 7)) :=
  [ .inv a ⬝ .pow (c ⬝ d) 4,
    .inv a ⬝ .pow (f ⬝ g) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ b ⬝ c ⬝ f) 5,
    .pow (b ⬝ f ⬝ g) 5,
    .pow (.pow (b ⬝ c ⬝ d ⬝ c ⬝ d) 5 ⬝ e) 3,
    .pow (a ⬝ b ⬝ c ⬝ g) 5 ]

/-- The Group Presentations Library finite presentation `GPLTable.Suz.1` of the Suzuki sporadic
group on generators `a`, `b`, `c`, `d`, `e`, `f`, and `g`.

The source describes this as a full presentation of the abstract group and identifies its origin
as Praeger--Soicher. No structural property of the presented group is asserted here: this
definition records only the cited generators and relations. -/
def suzPresentation : GroupPresentation where
  generatorNames := ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g"]
  source := "R. Lindenbergh, Group Presentations Library, version 1.0; presentation attributed \
    there to C. E. Praeger and L. H. Soicher, Low Rank Representations and Graphs for Sporadic \
    Groups, Cambridge University Press, 1997"
  sourceLocator := "GPLTable.Suz.1 in \
    https://doris.tudelft.nl/~rlindenbergh/GPL/gpl.g; Praeger--Soicher, Chapter 4, \
    doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526039.005"
  generatorConvention := "Generators have source order a,b,c,d,e,f,g, so indices 0 through 6 \
    have those names. A Coxeter path declares each node to be an involution, a labeled edge x-m-y \
    declares (x*y)^m = 1, and an omitted edge declares (x*y)^2 = 1. Products are read left to \
    right. The source decoder compiles x = y as x^-1*y."
  transcriptionNotes := "Expand the paths a5b3c8d3e and b3f4g3b to seven square relations, \
    seven labeled-edge relations, and fourteen omitted-edge relations. Append the five words in \
    presdef[3], compiling the two equalities by the source's MakeWordList decoder, and the one \
    word in presdef[4]. The latter is present because InitializeGroupPresentationGPL includes \
    presdef[4] when GPL_PCE is true, as it is by default in version 1.0. The expected relator \
    count and total length are derived from this exact expansion. An independent read-through of \
    GPLTable.Suz.1 and its DeCoxList, MakeWordList, and InitializeGroupPresentationGPL decoders \
    checked the generator order, both paths, all six appended relations, and the compiled signed \
    letters; the itemized comparison is recorded in this module's independent audit section. GAP \
    4.15.1 enumerates 1782 cosets of the subgroup generated by a through f, which the source \
    labels G2(4). An independent comparison transports the resulting 1782-point action to the \
    graph in finite-simple-groups-lean at commit 7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325 and \
    checks mutual generator membership with that construction of Suz; the comparison is recorded \
    in this module's independent audit section."
  expectedGeneratorCount := 7
  expectedRelatorCount := 34
  transcribed := suzCoxeterRelators ++ suzAdditionalRelators

/-- The generator names recorded for `Suz`. -/
@[simp]
theorem suzPresentation_generatorNames :
    suzPresentation.generatorNames = ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g"] := by
  rfl

/-- The source recorded for `Suz`. -/
@[simp]
theorem suzPresentation_source :
    suzPresentation.source = "R. Lindenbergh, Group Presentations Library, version 1.0; \
      presentation attributed there to C. E. Praeger and L. H. Soicher, Low Rank \
      Representations and Graphs for Sporadic Groups, Cambridge University Press, 1997" := by
  rfl

/-- The locator recorded for `Suz`, including the source's identifier for this presentation. -/
@[simp]
theorem suzPresentation_sourceLocator :
    suzPresentation.sourceLocator = "GPLTable.Suz.1 in \
      https://doris.tudelft.nl/~rlindenbergh/GPL/gpl.g; Praeger--Soicher, Chapter 4, \
      doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526039.005" := by
  rfl

